;
; How Commons indexes one message in MYRA (commons_rules.h CR5): its room
; (3 digits) and its place there (pos: the feed's rank or the space's event
; index, 12 digits), its Lamport time (18 digits), when it was written in
; ms since 1970 (13 digits, to the year 2286) and its length in bytes (4
; digits). Commons asks whether the numbers fit before it keeps a message.
^ZXCOMMONSMSG(room:i3, pos:i12) = lamport:i18! ^ stamp:i13! ^ bytes:i4!
